# PL-16, L §6.4. Its items: "Two scenarios over one base never meet, so each may declare an id the other declares":
# t1 and t2 each declare the input bonus and the ask c (10.00 and 20.00 PLN). from D: "a scenario row over a base fact
# that governs always governs only from D, and in that world the fact changes with the law date: its readers there
# state their law date (§4.3, P-6)": k governs always in the base, read without a law date there (q); in u1 it is 2
# from 2027-01-01 and 1 before (r, r0); u2's ask reads it without one (LOAD-LAWDATE), refusing u2 alone (L §8.3).
=== b.tally
model base
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2030-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input k: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  k = 1 "s"

ask q: k
=== tb1.tally
scenario t1 over base
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

input bonus: money PLN

version b1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-10-15
  bonus = 10.00 PLN "own"

ask c: bonus in t1
=== tb2.tally
scenario t2 over base
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

input bonus: money PLN

version b2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-10-15
  bonus = 20.00 PLN "own"

ask c: bonus in t2
=== u1.tally
scenario u1 over base
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version w1
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-10-15
  replace k = 2 "s"

ask r: k in u1 law 2027-06-01
ask r0: k in u1 law 2026-06-01
=== u2.tally
scenario u2 over base
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version w2
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-10-15
  replace k = 3 "s"

ask r2: k in u2
=== expect
scenario u2: refused: LOAD-LAWDATE ask r2 reads law-dated k directly, without law (u2.tally:11)
c: 10.00 PLN
  world: t1
  cut 2026-10-20
c: 20.00 PLN
  world: t2
  cut 2026-10-20
q: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
r: 2
  world: u1
  held: k = 2 (w1), read for 2027-06-01
  law date 2027-06-01, cut 2026-10-20
r0: 1
  world: u1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-10-20
